==Translingual==
A character of the braille script, standardized internationally as the letter ''a'' and the digit ''1''.

===Etymology===
{{Brai-ety}}

===Letter===
{{mul-letter|sc=Brai}}

# {{lb|mul|Braille}} [[a]]
# {{lb|mul|Braille|often preceded by capital sign [[⠠]]}} Upper-case [[A]]
# {{lb|mul|Greek Braille}} {{l|mul|α|sc=Grek|tr=a}}
# {{lb|mul|Yugoslav Braille}} {{l|mul|a|sc=Latn}} / {{l|mul|а|sc=Cyrl}}
# {{lb|mul|Russian Braille}} {{l|mul|а|sc=Cyrl|tr=a}}
# {{lb|mul|Hebrew Braille}} {{l|mul|sc=Hebr|א|tr=aleph: ’}}
# {{lb|mul|Arabic Braille}} {{l|mul|ا|sc=Arab|tr=alif: ʾ}}
# {{lb|mul|Bharati braille}} ''a'' (only written when initial in a word); {{l|mul|अ}} / {{l|mul|ਅ}} / {{l|mul|અ}} / {{l|mul|অ}} / {{l|mul|ଅ}} / {{l|mul|అ}} / {{l|mul|ಅ}} / {{l|mul|അ}} / {{l|mul|அ}} / {{l|mul|අ}}
# {{lb|mul|Tibetan Braille}} {{l|mul|ཨ|tr=a}}
# {{lb|mul|Chinese Braille}} Tone 1
# {{lb|mul|Chinese Two-Cell Braille}} The onset ''g-'' or the rime ''-èn (-ìn, -ùn, -ǜn)''
# {{rfv-sense|mul}} {{lb|mul|Taiwan Braille}} Tone 0, onset ''zh''<!--this is in our source on WP, but there are other possible errors, and no other character has two readings like this-->
